WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.811
Here is the Shuttle board, and how to use its main controls.

2
00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:12.101
The Desk shows what is waiting on you, what is working, and results awaiting review, with drafts and resting cards on the shelf below.

3
00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:17.103
To write a task yourself, click the plus button to open the Stash form.

4
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:23.170
The Stash form asks for a title, optional details, a project and an agent.

5
00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.374
One-shot is a single task. Standing repeats on a schedule.

6
00:00:27.524 --> 00:00:30.593
With One-shot selected, Stash saves a draft card.

7
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.801
Or click the star on Working, and describe an idea in your own words.

8
00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:39.158
Pick a project and press Spawn.

9
00:00:39.308 --> 00:00:43.604
An agent turns your words into a task, and its card appears a moment later.

10
00:00:44.733 --> 00:00:46.942
Click any card to open its reader.

11
00:00:47.092 --> 00:00:52.581
The console under its title shows who works it, opens its conversation, and holds its controls.

12
00:00:52.731 --> 00:00:56.267
Write a message for the worker if you like, then choose how to send it.

13
00:00:56.417 --> 00:01:01.172
New session starts a fresh conversation, which reads the task and its notes from the top.

14
00:01:01.322 --> 00:01:04.899
If a worker is still running, the board asks before cutting it off.

15
00:01:05.049 --> 00:01:08.086
Resume requests the task’s previous conversation.

16
00:01:08.236 --> 00:01:10.919
Use it when finished work needs one more change.

17
00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:20.558
In Working, click a live row to read its progress or open its terminal conversation in Rex, tmux, or a browser.

18
00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.006
When a worker finishes, its card moves to Awaiting review.

19
00:01:25.156 --> 00:01:30.008
Read its outcome, then press Temper to accept the result, or Discard to set it aside.

20
00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:36.899
To try it, open the setup and tutorial page, and let your agent guide you through one small task.
